Then it is important clearly communicate what your changes do. If its a UI change make sure to include a screenshot, if its code like this write all relevant input cases for the function (e.g. entering 0 minutes, 1 minute, 30 minutes, 70 minutes, and likely something with more than 24 hours) and show that it does for each case what it is supposed to do. This way the maintainer does not need to go into a javascript console themself and test out all those cases and can quickly see that the suggested change is working as intended. Optionally many maintainers expect that you quickly elaborate on considered alternatives and a small explanaition on why you decided to implement something the way you did (probably not on something as simple as this but if you start doing bigger contributions)

